A||||2||boutip||Overcharging condition
Z||000000||boutip||06-20-99||03:47 PM||||I have an 88GT which exhibits an overcharging condition. At start up the gauge reads about 18 volts. I took the alternator out and had it tested at a reputable rebuild shop. The alternator tested fine. Does anyone have any other idea what could be causing me this condition. The guy at the shop mentioned that he has seen a couple of wacky conditions similar to this that were caused by a faulty fusible link in the battery compartment area.<br>Any help is appreciated.<br>
Z||000001||theogre||06-20-99||07:27 PM||||with the car running place a good digital volt meter across the batery terminals. The voltage should be between 13.5-15 VDC. Don't depend on a dash gauge alone for this, it could be off for a number of reasons.
Z||000002||lowCG||06-20-99||11:59 PM||||I've seen faulty batteries that have caused effects like you have described;car still starts,runs.<br>One strange possibility anyways.<br>Curious to hear what happens when you test for volts the way thee Ogre hath described.<br>
